concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-28b-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "28B(6) Unfair trading practices towards consumers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-28b-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) Without limiting subsection (2), the following are examples of conduct that may be unfair trading practices:  (a) impeding the consumer’s ability to exercise legal rights, or seek legal remedies;  (b) failing to disclose material information to the consumer;  (c) disclosing material information to the consumer in a complex, ineffective, unclear, unintelligible, ambiguous, untimely or overwhelming way;  (d) creating an environment (including by using design elements in digital interfaces) which places the consumer under unreasonable pressure in relation to, or obstructs the consumer from, making or fulfilling the consumer’s decision." ;
    skos:definition "(6) Without limiting subsection (2), the following are examples of conduct that may be unfair trading practices:  (a) impeding the consumer’s ability to exercise legal rights, or seek legal remedies;  (b) failing to disclose material information to the consumer;  (c) disclosing material information to the consumer in a complex, ineffective, unclear, unintelligible, ambiguous, untimely or overwhelming way;  (d) creating an environment (including by using design elements in digital interfaces) which places the consumer under unreasonable pressure in relation to, or obstructs the consumer from, making or fulfilling the consumer’s decision."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5d71c907d6015c7366571f0c4c42e5f8f6c6a8f60849f5196a98af002fd17805" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-28b ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Examples of conduct that may be unfair trading practices towards consumers." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
