concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "48B Subscription contracts"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-48b ;
    values:originalText "(1) A contract is a subscription contract if it:  (a) meets the requirement in subsection (2), (3), (5) or (6); and  (b) is not an excluded subscription contract. Note: A contract may meet the requirement in more than one of subsections (2), (3), (5) and (6). Indefinite period  (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), the requirement is that the contract contains terms that have the effect of providing:  (a) for recurring or continuing supply of goods or services for an indefinite period; and  (b) for a person to automatically incur liability to pay for the supplies or continuing supply; and  (c) a right for that person to end the contract. Fixed period  (3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), the requirement is that the contract contains terms that have the effect of providing:  (a) for supply of goods or services in, or recurring or continuing supply of goods or services for, a fixed period; and  (b) for supply, or continuing supply, of goods or services to continue after the end of the fixed period unless a party to the contract stops the supply or continuing supply or the contract is terminated; and  (c) for a person to automatically incur liability to pay for the supplies or continuing supply; and  (d) a right for that person to end the contract.  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A contract is a subscription contract if it:  (a) meets the requirement in subsection (2), (3), (5) or (6); and  (b) is not an excluded subscription contract. Note: A contract may meet the requirement in more than one of subsections (2), (3), (5) and (6). Indefinite period  (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), the requirement is that the contract contains terms that have the effect of providing:  (a) for recurring or continuing supply of goods or services for an indefinite period; and  (b) for a person to automatically incur liability to pay for the supplies or continuing supply; and  (c) a right for that person to end the contract. Fixed period  (3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), the requirement is that the contract contains terms that have the effect of providing:  (a) for supply of goods or services in, or recurring or continuing supply of goods or services for, a fixed period; and  (b) for supply, or continuing supply, of goods or services to continue after the end of the fixed period unless a party to the contract stops the supply or continuing supply or the contract is terminated; and  (c) for a person to automatically incur liability to pay for the supplies or continuing supply; and  (d) a right for that person to end the contract.  Schedule 1  Amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "94f9fbd29ade1d8dbf5265cba7198e4ce8ebaa61a86eb4e643c54297aebe03ab" ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48b-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48b-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026-sch-1-sec-48b-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-amendment-unfair-trading-practices-act-2026.pdf, p.15" .
doc:sch-1-sec-48b a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "48B Subscription contracts" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A contract is a subscription contract if it:  (a) meets the requirement in subsection (2), (3), (5) or (6); and  (b) is not an excluded subscription contract. Note: A contract may meet the requirement in more than one of subsections (2), (3), (5) and (6). Indefinite period  (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), the requirement is that the contract contains terms that have the effect of providing:  (a) for recurring or continuing supply of goods or services for an indefinite period; and  (b) for a person to automatically incur liability to pay for the supplies or continuing supply; and  (c) a right for that person to end the contract. Fixed period  (3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), the requirement is that the contract contains terms that have the effect of providing:  (a) for supply of goods or services in, or recurring or continuing supply of goods or services for, a fixed period; and  (b) for supply, or continuing supply, of goods or services to continue after the end of the fixed period unless a party to the contract stops the supply or continuing supply or the contract is terminated; and  (c) for a person to automatically incur liability to pay for the supplies or continuing supply; and  (d) a right for that person to end the contract.  Schedule 1  Amendments" ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer .

